  "result": "There is a particular stillness just before dawn, when the world seems to hold its breath. The streetlights are still on, but the sky has begun to lighten, bruise-blue and faint gold. I like to be awake for this part of the day, not because I am productive, but because it feels like borrowed time. Everyone else is asleep, and the city belongs to the few of us who are not: the runners, the insomniacs, the parents of small children, the people who have lost something and are trying to think clearly.\n\nI used to believe that meaning arrived in big pieces: a degree, a job, a relationship, a move across the country. I imagined life as a series of milestones that, once achieved, would finally explain themselves. But meaning is smaller and slipperier than that. It hides in the smell of coffee while rain hits the window, in a friend remembering a detail you mentioned once, in the courage it takes to apologize. It is not a destination. It is more like weather.\n\nWe are not, any of us, finished products. We are rough drafts, revised daily, full of crossed-out lines and awkward phrasing. That should be comforting. A rough draft still has potential; a finished thing can only be what it is.\n\nSo I am trying to be gentler: with myself, with the strangers whose whole stories I do not know, with the slow, uncertain process of becoming. The light is changing now. The birds have started. Another day is beginning, and it does not need to be perfect to be worth showing up for.",
